From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: i2c: slave-eeprom: add an OF match table for module autoload

A backend instantiated from the device tree (compatible "slave-24c02",
reg = <(I2C_OWN_SLAVE_ADDRESS | 0x64)>) gets an i2c client, but the
uevent of a client with an of_node carries an of: modalias
(of:N...Cslave-24c02). The module only declares i2c: aliases, so udev
never loads it and the client stays unbound: no slave-eeprom file and
no target registered, with nothing in the log. Only the sysfs
new_device path (i2c: modalias) or a manual modprobe worked.

Declare the same names as an OF table and export it, so the module
autoloads for DT and overlay clients. Matching and probe are
unchanged: the client name is the compatible without a vendor prefix,
so i2c_client_get_device_id() still finds the size and flags.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/i2c-slave-eeprom.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/i2c/i2c-slave-eeprom.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/i2c-slave-eeprom.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
+#include <linux/mod_devicetable.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
@@ -203,9 +204,29 @@
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(i2c, i2c_slave_eeprom_id);
 
+/*
+ * Firmware instantiates a backend with the I2C id as compatible and
+ * I2C_OWN_SLAVE_ADDRESS in reg (i2c-controller.yaml in dtschema).
+ * Such a client announces an of: modalias, so without this table the
+ * module never autoloads for it.
+ */
+static const struct of_device_id i2c_slave_eeprom_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c02" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c02ro" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c32" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c32ro" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c64" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c64ro" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c512" },
+	{ .compatible = "slave-24c512ro" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, i2c_slave_eeprom_of_match);
+
 static struct i2c_driver i2c_slave_eeprom_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "i2c-slave-eeprom",
+		.of_match_table = i2c_slave_eeprom_of_match,
 	},
 	.probe = i2c_slave_eeprom_probe,
 	.remove = i2c_slave_eeprom_remove,
